dm: LG's webos-verity target

LG's webOS TV kernels have a device-mapper target, webos-verity, that mounts a verity image which
carries its own table: an AOSP-style image (data, hash tree, metadata, FEC) whose metadata holds
the verity table and a PKCS#7 signature over it. apinstaller loop-mounts the adaptive partition
(appackage.pak) through it, and it cannot do without: it checks the target is registered.

This one reads the FEC header and the metadata as LG's does, checks the signature against the
certificates loaded through /proc/webos_verity_certs (the firmware kernel's own; sealed by an
empty write or the first table), and hands the table, with the options LG's kernel adds, to the
verity target, whose operations it shares. A bad signature refuses the table, where LG's kernel
restarts the set.
--- a/drivers/md/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/md/Kconfig
@@ -605,6 +605,20 @@
 
 	  If unsure, say N.
 
+config DM_WEBOS_VERITY
+	bool "LG webOS verity target"
+	depends on DM_VERITY=y && DM_VERITY_FEC
+	select SYSTEM_DATA_VERIFICATION
+	help
+	  The webos-verity target of LG's webOS TV kernels: a verity device
+	  whose table, hash tree and forward error correction come from the
+	  image itself, its table signed with PKCS#7. The table is verified
+	  against the certificates loaded through /proc/webos_verity_certs
+	  (the firmware kernel's own built-in ones) and handed to the verity
+	  target.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
+
 config DM_SWITCH
 	tristate "Switch target support (EXPERIMENTAL)"
 	depends on BLK_DEV_DM
